<resources>
    <!--
        The icon's background: the cream the logo is printed on.

        It was the React Native app's primary violet, #6C63FF, which was the right
        answer while the foreground was a white t-shirt and is the wrong one now —
        the mark is a taupe thread on cream, and putting it on violet would be
        using the logo's shape and none of the rest of it.

        Not a night variant, and it must not become one. This colour is read by the
        adaptive icon, and an icon that changed with the system theme would be a
        different icon on the same launcher twice a day. The splash screen, which
        does want to follow the theme, has its own colour next door in
        splash_background.xml.
    -->
    <color name="ic_launcher_background">#F3EDE3</color>
</resources>
